From: Martin Pluskal <martin@pluskal.org>
Subject: core: every EvalWorkflowSnippet asks for approval

prepareEvalWorkflowSnippetApproval() let any snippet without a world.run
call (and any that failed to compile) run without a prompt. A snippet is
code, compiled and run in a child node process inside node:vm, which
Node does not offer as a security boundary, and it can be read from a
file in the workspace. Without the hook the standard approval applies:
Build mode asks, the user's always-allow and yolo choices still hold.
prepareEvalWorkflowSnippetApproval() is left unused to keep this small.

Patch-mainline: No

--- a/apps/zcode-cli/packages/core/src/tool/handlers/eval-workflow-snippet.ts	2026-09-25 15:07:08.480403038 +0200
+++ b/apps/zcode-cli/packages/core/src/tool/handlers/eval-workflow-snippet.ts	2026-09-25 16:04:26.863421454 +0200
@@ -258,7 +258,8 @@
     riskLevel: "low",
     needsApproval: true,
   },
-  prepareApproval: prepareEvalWorkflowSnippetApproval,
+  // Every snippet asks: it runs code in a child node whose node:vm context
+  // is not a security boundary, and it may come from a file in the workspace.
   handler: evalWorkflowSnippetHandler,
   // 来源二选一只对模型入参成立；`path` 在归一化里读成 `code`，确认门与 handler 因此同形。
   validateInput: (input) => validateEvalWorkflowSnippetInput(input),
@@ -274,7 +275,7 @@
   permission: {
     permission: "evalWorkflowSnippet",
     reason:
-      "evalWorkflowSnippet.runConfirmation: snippets carrying world.run commands must be confirmed",
+      "evalWorkflowSnippet.runConfirmation: every snippet must be confirmed",
     riskLevel: "low",
     sideEffectScope: "workspace",
     needsApproval: true,
